Stellarena Privacy Policy
Last updated: 10/14/2026

This policy describes how the Stellarena iOS game ("the Game") handles information. The Game is developed by [Drake Robison] ("we", "us").

Summary
The Game does not collect personal data. Your progress is stored only on your device, and we do not receive it.

Information we collect
We do not collect, transmit, sell, or share personal information. The Game does not require an account or sign-in, and it does not send any data from your device to our servers or to third parties.

Information stored on your device
To save your progress, the Game stores the following on your device only: buildings and layout, resources, Crystal balance, campaign progress, settings, and a record of completed purchases. This data never leaves your device. Deleting the Game removes this data.

Purchases
In-app purchases (Crystal packs and Ship Pack 1) are processed by Apple through the App Store. We never receive your payment details, Apple ID, or other personal information about your purchase. Crystals are saved on your device and are not restored if you delete the Game. Ship Pack 1 can be restored with the Restore Purchases option in the Shop.

Analytics, advertising, and tracking
The Game does not include analytics, advertising, or tracking technologies, and it does not request App Tracking Transparency permission.

Children
The Game does not collect personal information from anyone, including children under 13.

Permissions
The Game does not request access to your contacts, location, camera, microphone, photos, or health data.

Changes to this policy
If this policy changes, we will update the "Last updated" date above and post the new version at this page.

Contact
For questions about this policy, contact: stellarena@ultraconsole.net
